Tinos 1.340, the outlines of Mill Serif (Regular, Bold, and Italic), kept in ../tinos.tar.xz so
Web Fonts can be rebuilt without a download. The three files are unchanged from the Google Fonts
build (name table: "Copyright 2026 The Tinos Project Authors", version 1.340), fetched on
2026-11-16 from google/fonts, ofl/tinos (raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/tinos/);
fonts.json lists each file's address and SHA-256, and build.py checks them. outlines.py reduces
them for Mill (Mac Roman only, no hints, 256 units per em) and build.py checks the results'
SHA-256 too.

Tinos is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, with no Reserved Font Name; the reduced fonts are a
Modified Version and stay under it. OFL.txt is the license as Google Fonts gives it for each
family: the font's own copyright line, then the license text (the same text as in its sister
families' OFL.txt files). It goes into Web Fonts (TXGZ 129) and its Read Me. Inside Mill the family
is called Mill Serif.
